- **`OwnerFields`** (openapi.yml line 1991): properties `firstName` (minLength 1, maxLength 30, pattern `^[\p{L}]+([ '-][\p{L}]+){0,2}$`), `lastName` (pattern allows trailing `.`), `address` (1–255), `city` (1–80), `telephone` (minLength 1, maxLength 20, pattern `^[0-9]*$`). All five `required`. → `OwnerFieldsDto` with getters/setters incl. `getTelephone()/setTelephone()`.
- **`Owner`** (line 2040): `allOf` OwnerFields plus read-only `id` (int32) and read-only `pets` array. → `OwnerDto`.
- Related generated DTOs referenced: `OwnerPageDto`, `ValidationMessageDto` (used by ProblemDetails/ValidationExceptionHandler).

Note: the `telephone` schema pattern is `^[0-9]*$` (any number of digits, so schema alone would allow "12345"); the exact-10-digit rule is enforced only by `ValidateOwnerFields.normalizeTelephone`.

## 8. Owner-related exception classes

Both in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/`:

- **`MissingOwnerFieldsException.java`** — `extends Exception` (checked). Ctor `MissingOwnerFieldsException(List<String> fields)`, message "Missing or blank required owner fields: …", exposes `getFields()`. Thrown by `ValidateOwnerFields`.
- **`NotFoundException.java`** — `extends Exception`, ctor `NotFoundException(String message)`. Generic not-found used by Load/Build functions elsewhere.

There is no `OwnerNotFoundException` specifically; the generic `NotFoundException` plays that role. There is currently no telephone-uniqueness/conflict exception, which is what Cp03 would require.

